# NewTOS native C toolchain — tracking policy.
#
# Each ported library (libc = mintlib, gemlib, cflib) vendors its PRISTINE source
# as a tarball; build-*.sh extracts it and overlays our edits (overlay/). The
# extracted tree, object files, and archive are build artifacts and are NOT
# tracked — the tarball + overlay/ + build script + tests ARE. A clone builds
# with no external network.

# Extracted source trees + build artifacts (regenerable via build-*.sh).
/libc/mintlib/
/libc/build/
/libc/libc.a
/gemlib/gemlib-0.44.0/
/gemlib/build/
/gemlib/gemlib.a
# ...and the same three for the m68k (real Atari) build of gemlib, which uses
# the PRISTINE source -- no NewTOS overlay -- because on m68k gemlib's own
# `trap #2` primitive is already the right one. See build-gemlib-m68k.sh.
/gemlib/gemlib-0.44.0-m68k/
/gemlib/build-m68k/
/gemlib/gemlib-m68k.a
/cflib/cflib-21/
/cflib/build/
/cflib/cflib.a
**/*.o
*.NCP
*.NAP

# App source trees under /apps/ stay vendored (big; third-party — QED compiles
# UNMODIFIED). Build scripts + tests directly in /apps/ ARE tracked. Our own LP64
# overlay edits live OUTSIDE the vendored (embedded-git) app trees, under
# sdk/overlays/<app>/, so they are tracked normally.
/apps/*/

# ...except apitest, which is OURS rather than vendored. Its T-numbered probes
# are the acceptance evidence for the desktop-rebuild stages, so losing them to
# a clean would lose the proof that a stage landed. Sources tracked, built
# binaries still excluded by the *.NCP rule above.
!/apps/apitest/
/apps/apitest/*
!/apps/apitest/*.c
!/apps/apitest/*.h
!/apps/apitest/*.sh

# ...and chaintest, likewise OURS: the .NAP that proves the AES shell loop
# actually executes a `shel_write` launch (stage S3 acceptance, audit finding
# P6-005). Same reasoning as apitest — it is the evidence a stage landed, so it
# must not be lost to a clean. Built binaries stay excluded by the *.NAP rule.
!/apps/chaintest/
/apps/chaintest/*
!/apps/chaintest/*.c
!/apps/chaintest/*.sh

# macOS junk that FAT round-trips create.
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.fseventsd
.Trashes
